WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.570
West Greenland.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:07.330
At Ilulissat Icefjord, icebergs break
from a calving front and crowd the fjord.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:12.290
Behind it lies an ice sheet of
1.7 million square kilometres,

4
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.650
over 3 kilometres thick.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:22.390
One outlet glacier, Jakobshavn Isbræ,
flowed 5,700 metres a year in 1992.

6
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.010
By 2003: 12,600.

7
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.830
More than double, in about a decade.

8
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.990
So what is in control here?

9
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.090
Warmer air?

10
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.610
The sea at the ice front?

11
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.090
The rock beneath?

12
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.570
In this mission, you'll follow the
ice from the dome to the fjord,

13
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.390
and the landforms it builds on the way.

14
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.550
Then you'll track how
the landscape changes,

15
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.230
from seconds to millennia.

16
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.600
Your mission: find out what controls
the landscape of an ice sheet.
